Subject: [PATCH] adaptivedemux: time the fragment bitrate from the first byte

The bitrate of a fragment is its size over the time since the request.
With small fragments the request latency is most of that time: a live
HLS stream with 2 s CMAF fragments of 30-90 KB and 50-200 ms until the
first byte measured 1-5 Mbit/s on a much faster line. The estimate
followed the size of the variant being played, so the stream stayed on
or fell back to the lowest variants.

Time the data from its first byte. A fragment that arrives at once
still counts a quarter of the download time.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/gst-libs/gst/adaptivedemux/gstadaptivedemux.c
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/adaptivedemux/gstadaptivedemux.c
@@ -2878,17 +2878,26 @@
         break;
       case GST_EVENT_EOS:
       {
+        GstClockTime data_time;
+
         stream->last_download_time =
             gst_adaptive_demux_get_monotonic_time (stream->demux) -
             (stream->download_start_time * GST_USECOND);
+        /* Calculate bitrate since the first byte: the request latency is
+         * most of the download time of a small fragment, the bitrate would
+         * follow the size of the variant being played. A fragment that
+         * arrives at once still counts a quarter of the download time. */
+        data_time = stream->last_download_time > stream->last_latency ?
+            stream->last_download_time - stream->last_latency : 0;
+        data_time = MAX (data_time, stream->last_download_time / 4);
         stream->last_bitrate =
             gst_util_uint64_scale (stream->fragment_bytes_downloaded,
-            8 * GST_SECOND, stream->last_download_time);
+            8 * GST_SECOND, data_time);
         GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (pad,
-            "EOS since download_start %" GST_TIME_FORMAT " bitrate %"
-            G_GUINT64_FORMAT " bps", GST_TIME_ARGS (stream->last_download_time),
-            stream->last_bitrate);
-        /* Calculate bitrate since URI request */
+            "EOS since download_start %" GST_TIME_FORMAT " first byte %"
+            GST_TIME_FORMAT " bitrate %" G_GUINT64_FORMAT " bps",
+            GST_TIME_ARGS (stream->last_download_time),
+            GST_TIME_ARGS (stream->last_latency), stream->last_bitrate);
       }
         break;
       default:
